&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/t/showdev"&gt;#showdev&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://dev.to/t/react"&gt;#react&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://dev.to/t/opensource"&gt;#opensource&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://dev.to/t/typescript"&gt;#typescript&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hey everyone! 👋&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'd like to introduce my new React component: &lt;strong&gt;React Tree Node View&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's a lightweight and customizable tree view component built with React and TypeScript, designed to make working with hierarchical data simple and intuitive.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌳 &lt;strong&gt;Two modes:&lt;/strong&gt; Editable and selectable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🖱️ &lt;strong&gt;Native drag-and-drop&lt;/strong&gt; for easy node reordering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;✏️ &lt;strong&gt;Inline title editing&lt;/strong&gt; and category management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🎨 &lt;strong&gt;Customizable icons, labels, and drop indicator colors.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌍 &lt;strong&gt;RTL and LTR support.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⚛️ Built with React and TypeScript, with no runtime dependencies besides React.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's now available on npm! 🎉&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Check it out
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-tree-node-view" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Tree Node View on npm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'd be happy to hear your thoughts, suggestions, or feedback. Thanks for checking it out! 😊&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For our Operations Research course at NMIMS Shirpur, my teammates and I wanted a tool that shows why each simplex step happens, not only the final answer. So I built &lt;strong&gt;OR/Studio&lt;/strong&gt;: a free, open-source Operations Research workbench that runs in the browser and works offline.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fhd3gsrpqbtcg9py9mne6.gif" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fhd3gsrpqbtcg9py9mne6.gif" alt="A real solve, stepped through" width="800" height="430"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What it does
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are 13 solver modules: simplex (including Big-M, two-phase and dual), integer programming, nonlinear programming, transportation, assignment, network models, project planning, queuing, inventory, game theory, Markov chains, simulation and job sequencing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every tableau and ratio test comes with a plain-language reason and the rule that was applied. In &lt;strong&gt;tutor mode&lt;/strong&gt; you pick the entering variable and leaving row yourself and get told what went wrong if you're off. In &lt;strong&gt;diff mode&lt;/strong&gt; you type your own working and it finds the first step where you diverged.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Exact arithmetic
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fractions are exact, so the numbers in a tableau match what you'd get by hand. Big-M and prohibited routes use a symbolic M, never a large number.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How I tested it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The solvers are pure TypeScript with no UI dependency, and I tested them against independent checks, not against themselves:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linear programs against vertex enumeration and strong-duality checks on random instances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integer programs and assignment against brute force.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transportation, max flow and games re-formulated as LPs and compared.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shortest-path and spanning-tree algorithms that must agree with each other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The repo has 452 tests. The hardest part wasn't the algorithms. It was the edge cases: unbounded problems, cycling, degenerate pivots and negative cycles.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What it doesn't do yet
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Separable programming isn't implemented, "Save as PDF" goes through the browser's print dialog, and the nonlinear module works in floating point. I've opened these as issues.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Live: &lt;a href="https://or-studio.antideploy.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://or-studio.antideploy.app&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code (MIT): &lt;a href="https://github.com/Jay-Naik2526/or-studio" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/Jay-Naik2526/or-studio&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'd like feedback from anyone taking or teaching an OR course, especially bugs and missing methods.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Usestate&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;UseState is one of the React Hooks used to manage state in a component.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Normally, when we use a local variable, changing its value does not trigger a re-render of the component.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But useState allows us to store a value and update the UI whenever that value changes. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Using a normal variable doesn't trigger a re-render the UI still doesn't show anything about your process by using a normal variable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To overcome this using usestate updates changes in UI everytime when the component gets re-rendered.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;const [stateVariable, stateFunction] = useState(0);&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Statevariable -It stored the current state value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;StateFunction - It is a setterfunction used to update the current state value. When called, it tells React to re-render the component so the UI can reflect the updated state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  Stop Treating Your App Mascot Like a Video: Build an Interactive Character With Rive
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;AI-generated animation clips are great for demos. But what happens when your app needs skins, levels, emotions, eye tracking, and real-time control?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI-generated mascot animations are everywhere.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can generate a character, create a few animation clips, and integrate them into your React app, mobile application, or SaaS dashboard.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a simple experience, that works.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But imagine your product grows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your mascot now needs to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React to different application states.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change skins without restarting its animation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Display user progression and level-up effects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Control eye direction and facial expressions independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to taps, achievements, and real-time events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve into different character forms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suddenly, your mascot isn't just an animation anymore.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It's an interactive component of your application's UI.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And that's where the architecture matters.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  1. The Problem With Clip-Based Mascots
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's start with a common implementation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You have five animation files:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;mascot/
├── idle.webm
├── happy.webm
├── sad.webm
├── sleeping.webm
└── celebrating.webm
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Your application switches between them based on user activity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A simplified React implementation might look like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;animations&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/mascot/idle.webm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;happy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/mascot/happy.webm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;sad&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/mascot/sad.webm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;celebrating&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/mascot/celebrating.webm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Mascot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;video&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;animations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;autoPlay&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;muted&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;playsInline&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This example is intentionally minimal. Production code would also need to handle looping, animation completion, loading, and transitions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But the general pattern is familiar:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Idle
  ↓
Happy
  ↓
Idle
  ↓
Celebrate
  ↓
Idle
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;For a simple decorative mascot, this may be completely sufficient.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, things get more complicated when the character needs multiple simultaneous properties.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What if the mascot should be celebrating while wearing Skin 3, looking left, and displaying Level 7 energy?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You either need more prepared assets or a more sophisticated runtime composition system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The limitation isn't necessarily AI generation. It's relying on fixed, pre-rendered clips for interactive product behavior.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  2. The Combinatorial Explosion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider a gamified learning application with the following requirements:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Feature&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Variations&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Emotional states&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Character skins&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Progression levels&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Facial variations&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you render every combination as a separate animation:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;emotions&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;skins&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;levels&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;faces&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;combinations&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;emotions&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;skins&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;levels&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;faces&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;combinations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 1200&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That's potentially &lt;strong&gt;1,200 animation combinations&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not necessarily 1,200 files in every implementation, of course. Layered rendering and reusable assets can reduce the number significantly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But if your architecture depends on unique pre-rendered clips, customization becomes increasingly expensive to maintain.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every new skin, level, or expression may require additional animation work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And now imagine adding:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eye tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mouth controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accessories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Different character forms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contextual reactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voice assistant interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is why character architecture should be considered early in product development.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  3. A Different Approach: Rive State Machines
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://rive.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Rive&lt;/a&gt; is a real-time animation tool and runtime that supports interactive vector graphics, reusable animation rigs, and state machines.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of exporting every character variation as a separate video, you can build a reusable character system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;                 APP LOGIC
                     │
                     ▼
              RIVE CONTROLLER
                     │
       ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
       │             │             │
       ▼             ▼             ▼
   EMOTIONS       APPEARANCE    PROGRESSION
       │             │             │
   Idle/Happy      Skin 0–4      Level 1–10
   Thinking        Outfit        Energy 0–100
   Celebrate       Character     Evolution
       │             │             │
       └─────────────┼─────────────┘
                     ▼
               CHARACTER RIG
                     │
                     ▼
              REAL-TIME OUTPUT
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The character can respond to multiple independent controls.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, a custom Rive state machine might expose:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Input&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Type&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Purpose&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;emotion&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Number&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Current emotional state&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;skin&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Number&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Selected character skin&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;level&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Number&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;User progression level&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;energy&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Number&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Energy or visual intensity&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;eyes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Number&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Eye expression&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;isTalking&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Boolean&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Talking mode&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Celebrate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Trigger&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One-shot celebration&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are &lt;strong&gt;custom inputs designed by the animator&lt;/strong&gt;, not built-in Rive input names.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your development team receives a documented contract describing what each input does.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's the important difference.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The mascot's behavior becomes part of the application's logic.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  4. React Integration: Controlling a Rive Mascot
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's look at a simplified React example using &lt;code&gt;@rive-app/react-canvas&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Install the package:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install&lt;/span&gt; @rive-app/react-canvas
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then load your Rive file and state machine.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useStateMachineInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@rive-app/react-canvas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MACHINE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;MascotController&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Mascot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;emotion&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;skin&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;level&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;RiveComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rive&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/mascot.riv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;stateMachines&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MACHINE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;autoplay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;emotionInput&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useStateMachineInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MACHINE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;emotion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;skinInput&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useStateMachineInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MACHINE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;skin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;levelInput&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useStateMachineInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MACHINE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;level&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;emotionInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nx"&gt;emotionInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;emotion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;emotion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;emotionInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;skinInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nx"&gt;skinInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;skin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;skin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;skinInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;levelInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nx"&gt;levelInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;level&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;level&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;levelInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;RiveComponent&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;240&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;240&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This assumes your &lt;code&gt;.riv&lt;/code&gt; file already contains the named state machine and numeric inputs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now the parent application can control the character:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Mascot&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;emotion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;skin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;level&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The Rive file decides how those values affect the visual character.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The React application decides when and why those values change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The developer controls the behavior. The animator defines how that behavior looks.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That separation makes collaboration much easier.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  5. One-Shot Animations and Completion Events
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not every animation should loop.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some actions should play once:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Celebrate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drink&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Level Up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React to Tap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A Rive state machine can expose triggers for these actions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, a &lt;code&gt;Celebrate&lt;/code&gt; trigger can play a celebration and return to the appropriate ongoing state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rive also supports runtime events, allowing the character to communicate information back to the application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A useful event contract might include:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;CelebrateComplete
EatComplete
DrinkComplete
LevelUpComplete
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This becomes especially useful in gamified applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine a character drinking from an energy container.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your application triggers the animation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The character finishes drinking.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A completion event notifies the application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The app updates its interface or continues the workflow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The animation is no longer just visual feedback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It becomes part of an event-driven interaction.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For reliable behavior, the state machine should also define what happens when users trigger multiple actions quickly, switch modes mid-animation, or repeat the same input.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  6. Skins, Levels, and Character Evolution
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is where a reusable character rig becomes particularly valuable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine a fitness app mascot with four visual forms:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Unlit
  ↓
Kindling
  ↓
Steady
  ↓
Radiant
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Each form represents a different stage of user progression.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The app also controls:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;level: 1–10
energy: 0–100
emotion: 0–7
skin: 0–4
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A properly designed character system can separate these concerns.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;level&lt;/code&gt; controls prepared progression visuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;energy&lt;/code&gt; adjusts glow intensity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;emotion&lt;/code&gt; controls facial expressions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;skin&lt;/code&gt; changes prepared appearance variations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;Celebrate&lt;/code&gt; triggers a one-shot reaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These controls can coexist.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You don't necessarily need a separate celebration video for every level, energy value, and skin combination.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You need reusable animations and a rig that supports those variations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are still practical limitations. A completely different outfit, silhouette, or character form may require additional artwork and rigging.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But reusable components help avoid unnecessary duplication.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  7. Think in Layers, Not Just States
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One of the biggest architectural improvements is separating character behavior into independent systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of thinking only about:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Idle → Happy → Idle
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Think about:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Character
│
├── Base Motion
│   ├── Idle
│   ├── Breathing
│   └── Body Movement
│
├── Facial Controls
│   ├── Eyes
│   ├── Eyebrows
│   └── Mouth
│
├── Emotions
│   ├── Happy
│   ├── Thinking
│   └── Sad
│
├── Appearance
│   ├── Skin
│   ├── Accessories
│   └── Character Form
│
├── Progression
│   ├── Level
│   ├── Energy
│   └── Evolution
│
└── One-Shot Actions
    ├── Celebrate
    ├── Wave
    └── Level Up
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Not every Rive project needs this entire structure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But planning around independent controls gives your character more flexibility as the product evolves.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The exact implementation may use state machines, nested artboards, data binding, reusable components, or a combination of supported Rive features.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The goal is to make the character predictable and controllable for developers.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  8. What About Performance?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A common question is whether Rive is always faster or smaller than video animations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The answer is no.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Performance depends on the actual assets and implementation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A simple compressed video may be more efficient for certain visual effects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A poorly optimized Rive file can also become expensive to render, particularly with complex vector geometry, effects, or excessive animation work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, Rive offers an important architectural advantage for interactive characters:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You can reuse character artwork and animations rather than exporting every variation as a separate pre-rendered clip.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For production apps, consider:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reusing character geometry and animations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avoiding unnecessary state-machine complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Testing on lower-end mobile devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeping visual effects appropriate for the target runtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting reduced-motion preferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measuring actual runtime performance and memory usage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Choose the rendering approach based on your product's needs, not just the file format.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  9. When Should You Use AI Animation vs Rive?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Requirement&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Fixed AI-generated clips&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Custom Rive mascot&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Simple idle animation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Great fit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Great fit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Marketing animation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Great fit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Possible&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Fixed celebration clip&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Great fit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Great fit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Independent eye controls&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Requires extra architecture&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Supported with custom rig&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Real-time facial expressions&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Limited in a fixed clip&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Supported with custom rig&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Multiple skins&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Additional assets/compositing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Reusable prepared variations&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Level-based evolution&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Additional assets/logic&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;State-driven progression&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Developer-controlled behavior&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Clip selection&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Runtime inputs and events&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Complex interactive mascot&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Requires custom systems&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Designed for this use case&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI-generated clips aren't inherently wrong.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;They solve a different problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your mascot is primarily decorative, a few animations may be all you need.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But if your mascot is part of the user experience, progression system, or AI assistant interface, a real-time interactive architecture is worth considering.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  10. Build a Character System, Not an Animation Gallery
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before integrating a mascot into your application, ask:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Will this character need new functionality six months from now?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your roadmap includes skins, progression, emotions, AI interactions, or personalization, consider building a reusable interactive mascot from the beginning.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At &lt;a href="https://mascotengine.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Mascot Engine&lt;/a&gt;, we create custom Rive mascots for:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React and web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobile apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SaaS products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI companions and assistants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gamified learning and fitness experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our work focuses on reusable character rigs, custom state machines, real-time developer controls, and integration-ready animation systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The goal isn't simply to make a character move.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's to give developers a character they can actually control.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Final Thoughts
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI can help you create a beautiful mascot animation quickly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But a beautiful animation isn't automatically an interactive character.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For simple experiences, pre-rendered clips are often enough.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For products that require real-time reactions, customization, progression, and developer-controlled behavior, think beyond the animation file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Don't build a gallery of mascot animations. Build a mascot system that can grow with your app.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're building a product that needs this kind of interaction, explore &lt;a href="https://mascotengine.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Mascot Engine&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;What approach are you currently using for animated characters in your apps: video clips, sprite sheets, Rive, or something else? I'd love to hear how you're handling interactive mascot behavior.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;useContext is used to avoid the props drilling in react.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It helps us to share the data from one component to another component directly without passing props through the intermediate component.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is done in 3 steps:&lt;br&gt;
                 1. createContext() - create a context&lt;br&gt;
                 2. Provider - provide the values&lt;br&gt;
                 3. useContext() - consume the values&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine you are building an order checkout system inside a Telegram Mini App using React. When a user opens your application inside their mobile client, Telegram injects an embedded WebView context exposing the global &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp&lt;/code&gt; object. React developers often jump straight into building UI components by pulling user profile details directly from &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp.initDataUnsafe.user&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you send this &lt;code&gt;initDataUnsafe&lt;/code&gt; user ID directly to your API to look up accounts, process orders, or issue rewards, your application is completely vulnerable to identity spoofing. Because Mini Apps are standard web applications running inside an embedded browser frame, anyone can open your Mini App's URL in a standard desktop browser, open Developer Tools, and mutate &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp.initDataUnsafe&lt;/code&gt; to contain any target user ID. An attacker can easily impersonate administrators or drain balances belonging to other users.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To secure your React Mini App, you must ignore &lt;code&gt;initDataUnsafe&lt;/code&gt; for authorization and treat the raw &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp.initData&lt;/code&gt; query string as an unverified credential. In this walkthrough, we will cover how to structure your React application lifecycle, perform server-side HMAC-SHA256 validation in Express, and safely control Telegram's native &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; without exposing unauthorized actions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Decoding the WebApp Context and Front-End Initialization
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When integrating Telegram with React, developers often struggle between using the official script tag or installing third-party wrapper packages like &lt;code&gt;@twa-dev/sdk&lt;/code&gt;. While wrapper packages offer TypeScript interfaces, third-party libraries frequently fall behind official Telegram Bot API feature releases. The most reliable approach is referencing the official script in your &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt; file while declaring type definitions for &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp&lt;/code&gt; in your codebase.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add the official Telegram WebApp script inside your public HTML entry point:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- index.html --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="cp"&gt;&amp;lt;!DOCTYPE html&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;lang=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"en"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;head&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;meta&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;charset=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"UTF-8"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;meta&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"viewport"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;content=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;title&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Mini App&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/title&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;script &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;src=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"https://telegram.org/js/telegram-web-app.js"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/head&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;body&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"root"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/body&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/html&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Telegram provides two distinct properties on &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;initDataUnsafe&lt;/code&gt;: An unverified JavaScript object parsed directly by the client browser. It contains fields like &lt;code&gt;user&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;auth_date&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;query_id&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;hash&lt;/code&gt;. Because this object exists in mutable client memory, it provides zero security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt;: A raw, URL-encoded string of parameters sent by Telegram's launch context. It contains key-value pairs representing the exact payload before client-side parsing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An example &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; raw string looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;query_id=AAG...&amp;amp;user=%7B%22id%22%3A987654321%2C%22first_name%22%3A%22Alice%22%7D&amp;amp;auth_date=1710000000&amp;amp;hash=a1b2c3d4...&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;hash&lt;/code&gt; inside this string is an HMAC-SHA256 signature calculated by Telegram using a secret key derived from your Telegram Bot Token. The front-end cannot alter any value inside &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; without breaking the hash. Your React application must pass this raw string to your API server inside an HTTP header (such as &lt;code&gt;Authorization: Bearer &amp;lt;initData&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;) on every initial load.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/services/api.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;verifyAndFetchUserSession&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rawInitData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/api/auth/verify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Content-Type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;application/json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Authorization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`TelegramInitData &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rawInitData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Authentication failed: Invalid Telegram signature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  Implementing Server-Side HMAC SHA-256 Validation in Express
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To verify that the payload originated from Telegram and was not altered by a proxy or client console script, your backend must perform the cryptographic verification procedure specified in the Telegram Bot API documentation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The algorithm requires these steps:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parse the raw URL-encoded &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; string into key-value pairs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extract and remove the &lt;code&gt;hash&lt;/code&gt; key from the key-value pairs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sort all remaining key-value pairs alphabetically by their keys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Format the sorted key-value pairs into a newline-separated string in the format &lt;code&gt;key=value\nkey=value&lt;/code&gt;. Telegram designates this string as the &lt;code&gt;data_check_string&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compute a secret key by taking the HMAC-SHA256 hash of your Bot Token string, using the constant string &lt;code&gt;"WebAppData"&lt;/code&gt; as the HMAC key.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compute the HMAC-SHA256 hash of the &lt;code&gt;data_check_string&lt;/code&gt; using the generated secret key.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compare the resulting hex digest against the client's &lt;code&gt;hash&lt;/code&gt; parameter using a constant-time string comparison function to prevent timing attacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify the &lt;code&gt;auth_date&lt;/code&gt; parameter to reject stale initialization strings. If &lt;code&gt;auth_date&lt;/code&gt; is older than your expiration threshold (e.g., 86,400 seconds or 24 hours), reject the request to prevent replay attacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is a complete Express authentication middleware implementing raw string verification using Node.js's built-in &lt;code&gt;crypto&lt;/code&gt; module:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// server/middleware/verifyTelegram.js&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;require&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;validateTelegramInitData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;authHeader&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;authorization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;authHeader&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;authHeader&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;startsWith&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;TelegramInitData &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;401&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Missing or malformed Authorization header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rawInitData&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;authHeader&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;substring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;TelegramInitData &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;URLSearchParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rawInitData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;receivedHash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;receivedHash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Missing hash parameter in initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Remove hash parameter before sorting&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Sort keys alphabetically and format into data_check_string&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;paramsArray&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Array&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;entries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;paramsArray&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sort&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;aKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;bKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;aKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;localeCompare&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;bKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dataCheckString&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;paramsArray&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;botToken&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;BOT_TOKEN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;botToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;BOT_TOKEN environment variable is not defined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Compute HMAC secret key derived from Bot Token using constant seed "WebAppData"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;secretKey&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createHmac&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;sha256&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;WebAppData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;botToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;digest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Compute HMAC hash of data_check_string&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;calculatedHash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createHmac&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;sha256&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;secretKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;dataCheckString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;digest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;hex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Perform constant-time equality check&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hashBuffer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Buffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;receivedHash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;utf-8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;calculatedBuffer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Buffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;calculatedHash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;utf-8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hashBuffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;calculatedBuffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;timingSafeEqual&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hashBuffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;calculatedBuffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;403&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Invalid cryptographic signature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Check auth_date for replay attack prevention (max age: 24 hours)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;authDate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;parseInt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;auth_date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentTime&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;floor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;maxAge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;86400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;authDate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentTime&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;authDate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;maxAge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;403&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;InitData payload has expired&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Parse verified user payload and attach to request&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userJson&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;telegramUser&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userJson&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userJson&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;module&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;exports&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;validateTelegramInitData&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  Safe React Lifecycle and MainButton Integration
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Telegram's native &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; renders inside the mobile client container outside your React DOM tree. Because &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; is controlled imperatively via global WebApp methods (&lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp.MainButton&lt;/code&gt;), improperly managing its state inside React components leads to broken event handlers and double-click actions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two critical implementation mistakes often break React Mini Apps:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Showing or enabling the &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; before backend initialization finishes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attaching &lt;code&gt;MainButton.onClick&lt;/code&gt; event listeners without clearing them in React's &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; cleanup return function, causing handlers to accumulate on every component re-render.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The proper architecture requires synchronizing backend authentication status with React state, initializing &lt;code&gt;Telegram.WebApp.ready()&lt;/code&gt;, and safely handling &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; click registration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is a complete checkout component demonstrating safe backend authentication and &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; binding:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/components/CheckoutApp.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;verifyAndFetchUserSession&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../services/api&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UserProfile&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;first_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;username&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;CheckoutApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;FC&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UserProfile&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setIsLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
